.TH ANTIGRAVITY\-UPDATE 1 "2026" "antigravity-update @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
antigravity\-update \- update a local Antigravity IDE installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B antigravity\-update
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares the version installed under the install directory with the newest one
published on \fBantigravity.google\fR. If the site is ahead, the new build is
downloaded, verified and rsynced into place.
.PP
The download is resumable, so an interrupted run can simply be repeated. Before
the archive is trusted its size is checked against what the server reported and
its table of contents is listed, because a truncated resumable download
otherwise looks like a success.
.PP
Installing writes to a system directory, so
.BR sudo (8)
may prompt for a password. Files the IDE writes itself are preserved across the
update, and the Chromium sandbox is restored to setuid root, without which the
IDE refuses to start.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Report the installed and available versions, then exit without changing
anything. Exits \fB3\fR when an update is available, which makes it easy to
drive from a script.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Do everything except the install itself: resolve, download, verify, extract.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Reinstall even when the installed version is already current.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep the downloaded archive instead of deleting it once the install succeeds.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Install directory. Default \fB/usr/share/antigravity\-ide\fR.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Already up to date, or updated successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Something went wrong.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, or a required program is missing.
.TP
.B 3
With
.BR \-\-check :
an update is available.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANTIGRAVITY_INSTALL_DIR
Same as
.BR \-\-dir .
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask whether an update exists, without installing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
antigravity\-update \-\-check
.EE
.RE
.PP
Only act when there is something to do:
.PP
.RS
.EX
antigravity\-update \-\-check || antigravity\-update
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update\-every\-thing (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @MAINTAINER@.
